\par\par \b \uc2 EQS-News: AI in satellite manufacturing: OHB Partners with Schwarz Digits\b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 13:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires German\par \uc2 RTDJGE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EQS-News: \f28 \uc2 \f2 OHB SE\f28 \uc2 \f2  / Key word(s): Alliance \par AI in satellite manufacturing: OHB Partners with Schwarz Digits \par 2026-06-29 / 13:37 CET/CEST \par The issuer is solely responsible for the content of this announcement. \par  \par =---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \par Bremen, June 29, 2026. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (AI) is opening up new opportunities for industrialized satellite \par manufacturing. To leverage this potential, \f28 \uc2 \f2 OHB\f28 \uc2 \f2  is partnering with Schwarz Digits, the IT and digital division of the \par Schwarz Group. \par Schwarz Digits is currently building a state-of-the-art data center in L\u252\'00\'FCbbenau, in the Lower \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lusatia\f28 \uc2 \f2  region. Once the \par first three of a total of six modules are completed by the end of 2027, the facility will enable the secure and \par independent operation of large AI models. The project is thus specifically strengthening digital sovereignty in Germany \par and Europe. \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marco Fuchs\f28 \uc2 \f2 , CEO of \f28 \uc2 \f2 OHB\f28 \uc2 \f2 : "Europe must become more independent, resilient, and faster - and all of this is enabled and \par driven by AI and space technology. Space technology and AI are two of the defining megatrends of our time, and it is \par essential for \f28 \uc2 \f2 OHB\f28 \uc2 \f2  to align itself with strong partners." \par Dr. Alexander Schellong, Member of the Executive Board and Managing Director of the Institute for Cybersecurity and \par Digital Sovereignty at Schwarz Digits: "The New Space economy is a global growth market and is crucial for Europe's \par sovereignty. By combining our cloud, AI, and cybersecurity expertise with \f28 \uc2 \f2 OHB\f28 \uc2 \f2 's innovative strength, we empower the \par European space sector to process complex data streams in real time, create new business models, and at the same time \par retain control over critical value chains." \par As part of the partnership, \f28 \uc2 \f2 OHB\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be able to use the infrastructure of Schwarz Digits - both for satellite projects \par and for the industrialization of manufacturing processes. Potential applications include design optimization and the \par training of AI models for analyzing sensor data from large satellite constellations. \par Kristina Wagner, CTO and CDO of \f28 \uc2 \f2 OHB\f28 \uc2 \f2 : "The partnership with Schwarz Digits opens up new ways for us to deploy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial \par intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in satellite manufacturing in a targeted manner. Particularly promising areas include the processing of \par large data volumes, training AI models for onboard data processing in orbit, and the industrialization of our \par production. This collaboration not only strengthens our innovative capabilities but also contributes to technological \par autonomy in Europe." \par Contact: \par Media representatives: \par Marianne Radel \par Corporate Communications \par Phone: +49 421 2020 9159 \par Email: marianne.radel@ohb.de \par Investors and analysts: \par Marcel Dietz \par Investor Relations \par Phone: +49 421 2020 6426 \par Email: ir@ohb.de \par =---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \par 2026-06-29 CET/CEST Dissemination of a Corporate News, transmitted by EQS News - a service of \f28 \uc2 \f2 EQS Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par The issuer is solely responsible for the content of this announcement. \par The EQS