\par\par \b \uc2 HK Bourse: Announcement From \uc2 Hope Life Intl Holdings\b0\par\par\uc2 1,565 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 13:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     For full details, please click on the following link: \par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0629/2026062901707.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0629/2026062901707.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  and The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited \par take no responsibility for the contents of this announcement, make no representation as to \par its accuracy or completeness and expressly disclaim any liability whatsoever for any loss \par howsoever arising from or in reliance upon the whole or any part of the contents of this \par announcement. \par  \par     This announcement is for information purposes only and does not constitute an invitation or \par offer to acquire, purchase or subscribe for any securities of the Company. \par  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 HOPE LIFE INTERNATIONAL HOLDINGS LIMITED\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par (Incorporated in the Cayman Islands with limited liability) \par VOLUNTARY ANNOUNCEMENT \par LATEST BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT \par This announcement is made by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hope Life International Holdings Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  (the "Company") \par and its subsidiaries (the "Group") on a voluntary basis to update the shareholders and \par potential investors of the Company regarding the business development of the Group. The \par Group is actively seizing the global industrial transformation opportunities presented by the \par era of AI, and, through strategic upgrading, is gradually developing into a digitised platform \par enterprise driven by AI technology that empowers the global \f28 \uc2 \f2 One Person Company\f28 \uc2 \f2  ("OPC") \par entrepreneurial ecosystem. \par  \par     STRATEGIC COOPERATION FRAMEWORK AGREEMENT \par  \par     The board (the "Board") of directors (the "Directors") of the Company is pleased to announce \par that on 29 June 2026 (after trading hours of the Stock Exchange), the Company entered into a \par strategic cooperation framework agreement with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Artificial Intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Development Group \par (Hong Kong)* ("AI Development Group") and its authorised entity for OPC business, Super \par Hezi (Xiamen) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Artificial Intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Co., Ltd.* () \par ("Super Hezi"), in relation to the relevant matters of jointly establishing a global OPC \par ecosystem alliance ("WOPC") global entrepreneur platform with Samoa as the financial hub, \par leveraging Super Hezi's global OPC cooperation network, technological capabilities and \par relevant authorised resources, and gradually building a global decentralised digital financial \par centre ("Cooperation Matters"). \par  \par     To the best of the Directors' knowledge, information and belief, having made all reasonable \par enquiries, each of AI Development Group, Super Hezi and their ultimate beneficial owners is \par an independent third party. \par  \par     *   For identification purposes only \par -1- \par COOPERATION MATTERS \par Pursuant to the strategic cooperation framework agreement, the Company and AI Development \par Group will, with Samoa as the financial hub, leverage Super Hezi's global OPC cooperation \par network and WOPC brand authorisation to jointly build the WOPC Global Entrepreneur \par Platform. Super Hezi will license its global OPC cooperation network, technology toolchain, \par financial data compliance and enterprise service capabilities to a joint venture, which, \par combined with the Company's Samoa and listing platform resources, will form a six-in-one \par OPC full-ecosystem empowerment system encompassing "technology + finance + data + \par business + compliance + enterprise services". \par  \par     The cooperation will be advanced in four phases driven by scenarios: (1) Ecosystem Entry \par Phase: with the WOPC Global Entrepreneur Platform as the core entry point, to aggregate \par global OPC entrepreneurs and provide services including AI tools, computing power, business \par schools, order matching and global supply chains, rapidly creating a network effect among \par entrepreneurs and helping 100,000+ OPCs to conduct global business; (2) Infrastructure Phase: \par led by AI Development Group to build six core system platforms, covering AI agent engines, \par cross-border e-commerce systems, smart contract platforms, digital identity authentication, \par compliance risk control and enterprise service middleware, providing underlying technology \par and financial infrastructure for the OPC ecosystem; (3) Platform Operations Phase: by \par connecting early-stage investment, domestic and overseas compliant digital channels and OPC \par lightweight listing channels, to continuously empower the growth of OPC enterprises through \par a mature three-stage, nine-step gradient system, achieving value creation and distribution \par within the ecosystem; (4) Global Expansion Phase: expanding to Hong Kong, international \par markets, Mainland China and overseas collaborative nodes, leveraging the dual-centre \par architecture to empower and assist Samoa in building a global hub for digital nomads, the \par world's leading decentralised offshore digital financial centre, continuously consolidating the \par Group's strategic positioning as the first stock in the OPC ecosystem platform sector. \par  \par     The Company and AI Development Group propose to establish joint venture companies in \par Mainland and overseas, adopting a "Mainland joint venture + overseas joint venture" dual- \par track model. The joint ventures will serve as a business vehicle for the complementary \par advantages of both parties, and also as a proving ground for the Group's organisational \par transformation. Upon verification of the AI financial business model, the learnings will \par gradually feed back into the Group's strategic upgrading and organisational evolution. \par  \par     In order to support the above business development, the Company will establish a core \par management team with expertise in AI and finance. In the first phase, a Chief Executive \par Officer will be appointed to oversee the overall planning and execution of the Group's AI \par financial strategy and to gradually establish a product and research department and a user \par growth centre, driving the Group's fundamental transformation from traditional industrial \par operations to AI-native platform operations. \par  \par     -2- \par INFORMATION ABOUT AI DEVELOPMENT GROUP AND SUPER HEZI \par AI Development Group is a globally leading AI and blockchain technology group, possessing \par core proprietary intellectual property including a complete blockchain technology foundation, \par digital exchange and cross-border payment systems. The Group has established in-depth \par cooperation with leading companies in AI, computing power, cross-border business and \par investment, including Alibaba Cloud, ByteDance, Tencent Cloud, ARIS, HICUSTOM, \par G-bits, China Mobile, China Telecom and China Unicom, forming a full-stack empowerment \par capability of "AI + ecosystem + services". \par  \par     The Group comprises three principal business entities, responsible for blockchain underlying \par technology R&D and Guolian business, AI product development and system integration, and \par OPC ecosystem operations and global network management, respectively. Among them, Super \par Hezi is the sole authorised entity for the global OPC business of AI Development Group. \par  \par     Super Hezi is an AI enterprise based on A2A and DAO governance, dedicated to building an \par intelligence-empowered, decentralised cooperation and evolution network globally. Its core \par positioning is as the world's leading carbon-silicon fusion carrier platform. Its Super Hezi \par OPC Symbiosis Community is an evolution cradle for OPCs in the AI era, a "carbon-silicon \par fusion" life system with AI Native as its core engine and DAO+A2A as its cooperation network. \par  \par     REASONS FOR AND BENEFITS OF THE COOPERATION \par The Group is principally engaged in (i) construction and ancillary services; and (ii) consumer \par products business. \par  \par     In the face of structural transformation in the global AI industry, the Board believes that the \par Group must proactively upgrade its strategic positioning to seize the historic opportunity of \par empowering global micro-entrepreneurs in the AI era. The core logic of the Cooperation lies \par in the deep coupling and complementarity of the respective advantages of both parties. \par  \par     As a listed company in Hong Kong, the Company possesses international capital channels \par and a mature governance framework, and coordinates Samoa's offshore financial supporting \par resources to provide a compliant financial infrastructure for the global OPC ecosystem. \par  \par     AI Development Group and Super Hezi possess a complete AI and blockchain technology \par foundation, including proprietary intellectual property in digital exchange and cross-border \par payment systems. Super Hezi, as the operator of the global OPC cooperation network, has \par built a full-chain empowerment system covering technology, computing power, community, \par order matching and capital connection, and has obtained the WOPC brand authorisation, with \par the network effect to rapidly aggregate global entrepreneurs. \par  \par     Through the Cooperation, the Company and AI Development Group will establish joint \par ventures in Mainland and overseas, forming a dual-track parallel structure. The joint venture \par ventures will obtain exclusive operating rights to the WOPC brand to comprehensively \par build the WOPC Global Entrepreneur Platform, enabling Super Hezi to lead the rapid \par -3- \par implementation of OPC-specific ecosystem businesses in Mainland, while leveraging the \par Samoa node and dual-centre structure to build a global industrial platform integrating cross- \par border e-commerce, AI OPC platform and digital finance. \par  \par     On the financial and capital front, the R&D and operation and maintenance costs will be \par borne primarily by AI Development Group. The Company will receive revenue sharing from \par the joint ventures' overseas business and share in the ecosystem value of the global WOPC \par network. The Board believes that, through continuously empowering the growth of global \par OPC enterprises, the long-term strategic enhancement of the asset value of the listed company \par will be achieved. \par  \par     LISTING RULES IMPLICATIONS \par As the transaction contemplated under the strategic cooperation framework agreement is \par revenue in nature and conducted in the usual and ordinary course of business of the Group, \par the entering into of the cooperation framework agreement does not constitute a notifiable \par transaction under Chapter 14 of the Listing Rules. The cooperation framework agreement \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 29 Jun 2026 07:46 ET \par HK Bourse: Announcement From Hope Life Intl Holdings -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is a framework agreement only, outlining the cooperation intention, willingness and overall \par direction between the Group and AI Development Group. The Company hereby emphasizes \par that no specific terms have been reached on relevant Cooperation Matters. Further details on \par the Cooperation Matters are still under negotiation and will be determined by separate formal \par contract signed by both parties. If the two parties have reached clear terms of cooperation, \par the Company will carefully evaluate the impact and ensure full compliance with relevant \par requirements in accordance with Chapter 14 of the Listing Rules. \par  \par Source: Hong Kong Exchanges & Clearing \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 29, 2026 07:46 ET (11:46 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t001it\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
